{# Rendered via Base\Admin\Widget\WelcomeWidgetType (the "Generic" palette
   entry) - 'welcomeText' arrives as a template var (getTemplateVars()),
   either the custom params.text a superadmin typed in place or the
   original greeting default. No title: this widget's whole content IS
   the text, nothing else in it needs a heading to sit under (see the
   widget type's own comment on why getDefaultLabel() is never rendered
   here).

   data-widget-text is its own in-place-edit mechanism (see
   layout.html.twig's own input handler) - deliberately NOT data-analytics-
   title/data-brand-title: those two write straight into the widget's
   LABEL (a card title), this one writes into params.text (body content,
   no title concept here at all).

   Always carries the .card class now, same as every other widget type
   (analytics-card/composite-card/...) - the generic background toggle
   (see _block.html.twig's [data-toggle-background]) is a pure client-side
   class toggle on the WRAPPER (.widget-block.no-card-bg), applied on top
   of whatever the server already rendered - it never re-renders this
   template, so it can only ever show/hide a .card that's already in the
   DOM, not add one that isn't there yet. Conditionally omitting .card
   server-side (an earlier version of this comment/template) made the
   toggle button a dead click: it flipped the stored flag and the class
   on reload, but nothing visibly changed in the live preview before that
   reload happened. AbstractDashboardController::configureDashboardBlockItems()
   still sets this widget's own code-level default to false (not the
   generic MenuItem default of true), so a fresh/never-customized instance
   reads as part of the page itself, not a boxed widget competing visually
   with the real content cards around it - but a superadmin can now
   genuinely toggle a real card background on for it, live, same as any
   other widget. #}
<div class="widget-welcome card">
    <p class="dashboard-welcome" data-widget-text>{{ welcomeText }}</p>
</div>
